A hybrid framework of WGAN-GP and BiLSTM neural networks development. (A) Workflow of model construction. (B) BiLSTM architectures. (C) WGAN-GP architectures.

To ensure the Lipschitz continuity required by WGAN model, a gradient penalty (GP) is applied during training. This penalty ensures that the gradient norm of the critic with respect to its input remains close to 1, maintaining the stability of the model35. The penalty term is calculated using interpolated samples between original and generated data points, and a regularization coefficient of 10 is applied to control the strength of the penalty. The GP term is defined as the following Eq 1.1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
