Each variant was annotated with its original and mutated sequence, along with the mutation position. K-mer fingerprints were then computed using a standardized preprocessing pipeline and fed into a BiLSTM model previously trained to classify AVPs. The model was applied directly to predict activity probabilities for mutated sequences. The difference in predicted probability was calculated to quantify the functional impact of each substitution. To interpret the results, we classified each mutation into one of three categories based on its effect on predicted activity, quantified by the change in predicted probability (referred to as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
